meta {
  name: BankruptcyEstateAdministrator
  seq: 5
}

docs {
  # Bankruptcy estate administrator (konkursbo administrator) scenarios

  BDD scenarios for the enduser bankruptcy estate API at
  `/accessmanagement/api/v1/enduser/bankruptcyestate`.

  Feature: A bostyrer gives assistants access to all of their bankruptcy estates

    A bostyrer is a person holding the CCR role `bostyrer` (urn:altinn:external-role:ccr:bostyrer)
    for one or more bankruptcy estates (konkursbo). The bostyrer can make another person
    a bankruptcy estate administrator (role `innbygger-konkursbo-administrator`). The
    administrator then gets a rightholder connection from every estate of the bostyrer, with
    the packages hovedadministrator, konkursbo-lesetilgang and konkursbo-skrivetilgang.
    Revoking the role removes that estate access again.

    - GET  estates/any            does the party hold any bankruptcy estates
    - GET  administrators         the party's administrators and their estate access
    - POST administrators         add an administrator, identified by SSN or username and last name
    - DELETE administrators       revoke an administrator, identified by `user` (party uuid)
    - POST administrators/delete  the same revoke, for clients that cannot send DELETE

    Reads need the scope altinn:portal/enduser or altinn:bankruptcyestatedelegations.read,
    writes altinn:portal/enduser or altinn:bankruptcyestatedelegations.write, and the PDP must
    grant read or write on the resource altinn_bankruptcy_estate_admin for the party.

  Each subfolder is one scenario. The files inside are its steps, named
  `NN_GIVEN|WHEN|THEN|AND|CLEANUP_...` and ordered by `seq`. Every scenario starts from a
  known state and removes what it created, so the folder can run repeatedly against a shared
  environment and each scenario can run standalone.

  ## Personas

  Seed data comes from `testdata/bankruptcyestate-delegation/<env>.js`:

  - Bostyrer: BOSTYRER, a person who is bostyrer for a set of konkursbo and tvangsavviklingsbo.
  - Assistant: user_LUN_ANALYSE_GÅSTOL, the person made administrator and revoked again.
  - Outsider: creditor_VILJESTERK_GRANDIS, a person with no access to the bostyrer.
  - Organisation: creditor_GLAD_SLAPP_TIGER_AS, used where a person is required.

  admin_UGLESETT_FARMOR is left alone: it may be a standing administrator other tests rely on.

  ## Environments

  Runs in AT22 only for now. Every step skips itself when `tokenEnv` is not listed in
  `supportedEnvironments` in `helpers.js`; add an environment there once its seed data is
  verified.

  ## Failed person lookups lock the caller out

  Adding an administrator looks the person up by identifier and last name. Access Management
  counts failed lookups per authenticated user and, after `MaximumFailedAttempts` (2) of
  them, refuses every lookup by that user with 429 AM-00026 for
  `FailedAttemptsCacheLifetimeSeconds` (one hour). The counter lives in each pod's memory.
  Wrong last names and unknown persons therefore cannot run on every pass without breaking
  the bostyrer's own adds for the next hour, so `08_PersonLookupFailures` is opt-in; see its
  folder docs. The other validation scenarios only use inputs rejected before any lookup.
}
